---
export const prerender = true;
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import bookCover from '../../../images/shaping-future-innovation.jpeg';
---
<Layout title="Shaping the Future of Innovation" description="Volume overview for Artificial Intelligence: Shaping the Future of Innovation.">
  <section class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-4xl space-y-10 rounded-3xl bg-white/95 p-8 shadow-card sm:p-10">
    <header class="flex flex-col gap-6 md:flex-row md:items-center md:gap-8">
      <div class="flex-1 space-y-2">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-[#1b5ed8]">Overview</p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-display font-semibold text-[#113e8c]">Artificial Intelligence: Shaping the Future of Innovation</h1>
      </div>
      <figure class="w-full max-w-[190px] md:flex-none">
        <img
          src={bookCover.src}
          width={bookCover.width}
          height={bookCover.height}
          alt="Artificial Intelligence: Shaping the Future of Innovation cover"
          class="w-full rounded-3xl shadow-card"
        />
      </figure>
    </header>
    <article class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#113453]">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[#113e8c]">About this book</h2>
      <p>
        <em>Artificial Intelligence: Shaping the Future of Innovation</em> provides a concise non-technical introduction to artificial intelligence as the key driver of innovation in the new economy. The book positions AI as a General Purpose Technology, vital for driving advancements across all sectors of business, government, and society.
      </p>
      <p>
        Written for leaders, innovators, and decision-makers, this book bridges the gap between technical complexity and practical application, demystifying AI's core concepts while illuminating its catalytic impact across industries and organizations. Through a careful examination of innovation dynamics, computational foundations, and core AI principles, readers will gain the essential knowledge needed to both understand and effectively navigate the AI landscape.
      </p>
      <p>
        This succinct guide makes technical concepts accessible—from algorithms and machine learning to deep learning and generative AI—giving leaders the clarity they need to engage confidently with AI technology.
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-3">
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-[#1b5ed8]"></span>
          <p class="text-lg leading-7 text-[#113453]">Provides a thorough yet accessible introduction to AI</p>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-[#1b5ed8]"></span>
          <p class="text-lg leading-7 text-[#113453]">Emphasizes real-world applications and the ethical dimensions of AI</p>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-[#1b5ed8]"></span>
          <p class="text-lg leading-7 text-[#113453]">Provides a conceptual framework for leveraging AI to drive innovation across various sectors</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <article class="space-y-4 text-lg leading-8 text-[#113453]">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[#113e8c]">Author / Editor information</h2>
      <p>
        Alfred Essa has led pioneering AI and advanced analytics teams across academia and industry. As Simon Fellow at Carnegie Mellon University, VP of Analytics and R&D at McGraw Hill Education, and CIO at MIT's Sloan School of Management, he has consistently bridged the gap between theoretical innovation and practical implementation.
      </p>
      <p>
        His most recent book is <em>Practical AI for Business Leaders, Product Managers, and Entrepreneurs.</em> Essa has published more than 25 research papers spanning adaptive learning systems, risk analytics, and innovative approaches to data visualization using predictive model ensembles. He holds degrees from Haverford College and Yale University.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Layout>
